00:18:20.000 --> 00:18:25.000
and preserves every requested fact.

176
00:18:25.000 --> 00:18:30.313
A hallucination is plausible-seeming but
factually incorrect output that purports

177
00:18:30.313 --> 00:18:35.625
to assert something about the real world.
Even before a

178
00:18:35.625 --> 00:18:40.938
claim is proven false, an unsupported
claim should not be

179
00:18:40.938 --> 00:18:46.250
treated as established merely because it
is fluent. Tone is

180
00:18:46.250 --> 00:18:51.563
generated language, not a certificate of
accuracy. Words such as

181
00:18:51.563 --> 00:18:56.875
certainly, definitely, or probably do not
reveal a measured confidence

182
00:18:56.875 --> 00:19:02.188
score. For factual tasks, verify
individual claims against authoritative

183
00:19:02.188 --> 00:19:07.500
evidence, relevant tests, or checked tool
results. Record unknowns instead

184
00:19:07.500 --> 00:19:12.813
of filling them with likely-sounding
details. Match the review level

185
00:19:12.813 --> 00:19:18.125
to the consequences of error. The NIST
Generative AI Profile

186
00:19:18.125 --> 00:19:23.438
provides risk-management guidance for
generative AI. Our narrower practice is

187
00:19:23.438 --> 00:19:28.750
to trace each claim to supplied evidence.
The final mental

188
00:19:28.750 --> 00:19:34.063
model is simple: training adjusts
parameters; inference uses the trained

189
00:19:34.063 --> 00:19:39.375
model; prompts and context condition the
response; generation proceeds through

190
00:19:39.375 --> 00:19:44.688
token choices; and external evidence
establishes factual correctness. Better

191
00:19:44.688 --> 00:19:50.000
prompts clarify boundaries but do not
guarantee truth.

192
00:19:50.000 --> 00:19:55.000
You are ready to complete
activity-evidence-audit. Submit a

193
00:19:55.000 --> 00:20:00.000
