199
00:20:25.000 --> 00:20:30.000
Before the knowledge check, recap the five
objectives. Training adjusts

200
00:20:30.000 --> 00:20:35.000
parameters, while inference uses a trained
model with current input.

201
00:20:35.000 --> 00:20:40.000
Generation selects tokens repeatedly from
context. Tokens are model-specific units

202
00:20:40.000 --> 00:20:45.000
and are not necessarily words. Factual
claims can be supported,

203
00:20:45.000 --> 00:20:50.000
contradicted, or not established by
supplied evidence. A fluent unsupported

204
00:20:50.000 --> 00:20:55.000
answer should be corrected without
inventing what is missing. The

205
00:20:55.000 --> 00:21:00.000
eight questions also check context
windows, the toy lookup, fee

206
00:21:00.000 --> 00:21:05.000
evidence, workshop capacity, and
accessibility information. Review any

207
00:21:05.000 --> 00:21:10.000
section or the transcript before you
begin.

208
00:21:10.000 --> 00:21:15.000
Keep the shortest version with you:
training creates parameters, inference

209
00:21:15.000 --> 00:21:20.000
uses them, generation produces likely
continuations, and evidence determines

210
00:21:20.000 --> 00:21:25.000
factual support. Confident tone and
verified correctness are different

211
00:21:25.000 --> 00:21:30.000
properties. When a detail is missing, mark
it unknown or

212
00:21:30.000 --> 00:21:35.000
obtain evidence instead of guessing.
